oard\n4. **Fold (-1):** Not an option since checking is free\n\nReason:\n\nGiven the extremely dangerous board with 4 hearts, I should **check (0)**. While I have a decent two pair, the likelihood that my opponent has a flush is substantial. They called my turn bet and the river completed the potential flush. Checking allows me to:\n- Control pot size given the high risk\n- See if opponent bets (indicating strength)\n- Minimize losses if I'm beaten\n- Still win if opponent also checks with a weaker hand\n\nThis is a spot where pot control is crucial. Betting would only get called or raised by better hands (flush, full house, straight) and would cause worse hands to fold.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
